{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4043256d8ce6767d09a8896b7cfac7be1fd34f002eccdb48cb1186fec9ec38fa","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding metric backend","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_scc_files","rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize","_metric_invoke","_scc_files","scc --format json","--by-file","src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/scc_loc.py","tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff","Files array"],"problem_keywords":["metric detector","scc command","per-file entries","json output","file matching"],"propositions":["_metric_invoke invokes scc without --by-file flag, causing scc to return language summaries with empty Files arrays instead of per-file entries","_scc_files consumes the Files array from scc JSON output but yields no entries when Files is empty, preventing the threshold loop from executing and blocking any metric matches from being emitted","The metric detector can never emit file matches for code over the 800-LOC threshold because the scc command lacks the --by-file option required to populate per-file data","Adding --by-file to the scc invocation in _metric_invoke restores the ability to detect and emit normalized matches for files exceeding the configured LOC cutoff","Tool absence, timeout, nonzero exit, and invalid JSON remain fail-open evidence paths unchanged by the fix"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787304798788972751,"uuid":"f8689c60-fcd7-413d-8dc6-c4d1ac5a003d"}